hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2905","On the authority of Amir al-Shaabi, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the right of inheritance between the wife and the parents: For the wife, one-fourth of the total wealth, and for the children, one-third of it for the mother, and what is left is the father's share. (ie: wife's 1. mother's 1. and father will get two « kama mur anfa »)."
"2906","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: Sayyidna Umar (RA) used to find this problem easy wherever he went and we followed him. He decided that the problem would be four, one-fourth to the wife, one-third to the mother, and the remaining two parts to the father."
"2907","Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same as before in this chain of transmission."
"2908","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: May Allah not show me that I give priority to my mother over my father."
"2909","Ikramah said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) sent a message to Sayyidna Zaid Bin Thabit (RA) that you find a third of what is left for the mother in the Book of Allah (Holy Qur'an)? Sayyiduna Zaid (RA) replied: You are also a man, you give a fatwa about this with your opinion, and I am also a man and say it with my opinion."
"2910","Ata, may God have mercy on him, and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, both said in the matter of parentage with the husband: half of the wealth for the husband and one-third for the mother, and the child belongs to the father."
"2911","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said (in this matter): One-third of the total property belongs to the mother, whether the wife is accompanied by the parents or the husband is accompanied by the parents. \n That is: He has supported Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) in this issue."
"2912","Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: In the matter of wife and parents, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, opposed the people of Qibla, because he declared one-third of the total wealth for the mother."
"2913","Aswad bin Yazid said: Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a decision regarding the girl and the sister in Yemen and gave half of the property to the girl and the rest (as ``Isba'') to the sister."
"2914","It was narrated from Aswad bin Yazid that Sayyidna Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr (RA) did not give a share of inheritance to a real sister with a daughter until Aswad told him that Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA) gave half a share to the daughter and the rest to the real sister. told"
"2915","Bishr bin Umar said: I asked Ibn Abi al-Zanad: A man leaves a girl and a sister, how will it be divided? He said: His daughter will get half and whatever is left over will be given to his sister, and said that my father Al-Khajr bin Zayd reported that Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) used to consider sisters as Asaba with daughters, and would give them what was left of the inheritance from the heirs."
"2916","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated about the husband, mother and real and maternal brothers, he said: Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud and Sayyidna Zayd (RA) all used to share the inheritance with the brothers and Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: “The father makes the real brothers closer to the maternal brothers."
"2917","Al-Harith said: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) did not share with all the brothers."
"2918","Abu Majalz said: Sayyiduna Uthman used to share and Sayyidna Ali did not share."
"2919","Ibn Zakwan said: Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) used to share (all the brothers)."
"2920","Abdul Malik bin Umayr said: (Judge) Shareeeh used to participate."
"2921","Saeed bin Firoz narrated from his father that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said in the matter of polytheism: A father creates closeness among the three types of brothers."
"2922","Harith al-Awar said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) came to the issue of Banu Umm (cousins), one of whom was a maternal brother. He said: All the wealth will belong to the Akhiafi (maternal) brother, as if he had placed the maternal brother in the rank of a reckoning or real brother. Then when Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) came, I presented this issue to him and told him the decision of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him). He said: May God have mercy on him. So there were wise men (jurisprudents), but I will not give more than what Allah Ta'ala has made obligatory in this case, for that, the 60% will be divided like a man (see the explanation below for details)."
